  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Riches and Wonders** (1 review): Listener was moved to tears by this version of the song [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Blueberry Frost**: back after 53 archived shows (2348 days); rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **Alpha Double Negative: Going to Catalina**: rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **West Country Dream**: back after 44 archived shows (1212 days); rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **Riches and Wonders banter]**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Riches and Wonders**: back after 41 archived shows (983 days); rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **Orange Ball of Love**: back after 52 archived shows (2171 days); rare: 11 archived performances [4]\n- **Going to Port Washington**: back after 48 archived shows (1470 days) [4]\n- **Waving at You**: back after 25 archived shows (507 days); rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2005-07-02.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 16 songs; 51 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Sound periodically turns hollow because one PA channel kept dropping in and out; Recording is somewhat quiet, with fireworks popping audibly in the background [1][2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: requests/Orange Ball, touring [1]\n- Solo performance by JD on a rooftop in Brooklyn [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2005-07-02.flac16**: taped by Thomas Hartnett; transferred by Thomas Hartnett; source: AUD>Visivox SCM Broadcast Pro microphones>Visivox SCM preamp>Sharp MD-MT866 [1]. Also: Recorded to MiniDisc at a low level, then boosted and compressed in Sound Forge, adding some hiss and clipping [1]",
